  "answer": "I can't give you a figure for this. The RBA doesn't publish an Argentine peso (ARS) rate, and none of my data sources carry one.\n\nThe closest I can offer is the Australian dollar against the US dollar. On 16 October 2026, the latest reading, A$1 bought US$0.6947 (RBA, 4pm AEST).\n\nTo get pesos, multiply that by the USD/ARS rate. Argentina has had several different peso rates (official, \"MEP\" and \"blue\"), and they can differ noticeably. A$1 buys roughly 0.6947 × (the USD/ARS rate you choose). For a current figure, check Banco de la Nación Argentina or a currency converter.",
